 "caveats": [
  "NIMA residuals are computed against NIMA's own orbit solution, which absorbed the same astrometry -- this is a post-fit-residual channel, not an absolute ephemeris error.",
  "NIMA astrometry descends largely from MPC data plus dedicated runs, so independence from the comet lineages is partial.",
  "The in-cap detached-resident intersection is ~7 objects with a single out-of-cap resident control; the channel is registered as a pilot and cannot support a detection claim at this N.",
  "No occultation-anchor rows are distinguished in the omc_ast format; occultation ephemeris ties enter through the separate SOSB results database and are not folded in here."
 ]
